    "body": "Stacked on #2250, with #2513 on top. **All three PRs in this stack are meant to be merged together** \u2014 they are split for review only.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdopts the text-authored tutorial system from `probes-study-rebuilt` and converts all 25 lessons to it.\n\nEach lesson used to be an `.ml` file holding a serialized zipper alongside its prose \u2014 ~26,000 lines of generated data that had to be regenerated by hand for any edit. Lessons are now plain-text `.hzt` files in `hazel-programs/tutorial/`, embedded with `ppx_blob` via a new `src/tutorialslides` library (a clone of `src/docslides`) and parsed into `Tutorial.spec` at startup by `TutorialText`:\n\n```\n@title      the lesson name\n@flags      wrapper show_report version=N id=<uuid>\n@prompt     markdown for the instructions panel\n@hint       one-liner\n@reference  markdown for the Task Reference sidebar\n@hints      one per line\n@code       editor contents (holes are \u00bf, or ? to survive a container)\n@test       hidden tests\n```\n\nNet: **+2,855 / \u221226,285**.\n\nThe conversion was mechanical. `TutorialDecode` reads whatever lesson list is compiled in and emits `.hzt` via `MarkerParse.to_text`, so the CLI landed first and generated all 25 from the existing `Tu_*.ml`. `./hazel tutorial-verify` checks that each slide's impl and tests are a fixed point of `to_text \u2218 of_text \u2218 to_text`; all 25 are. `TaskRefDocs` is gone \u2014 decode inlines each lesson's composed `task_reference` into its own `@reference`.\n\nOne marker is ours rather than upstream's: **`@title`**. Upstream derives the title from the filename, which would renumber every lesson and mangle four of them (`Reverse Function Application (Pipelining)` losing its parens; `and`/`of` capitalising). `@title` pins the exact title and falls back to the derived one.\n\n## Bugs the round-trip check surfaced\n\n- **`$==` in the Case Expressions and Folding Lists hidden tests.** `$` does not lex in Hazel, so those six tests were unsatisfiable and always reported indeterminate \u2014 a live bug the serialized form hid. Now `==`, and both suites pass.\n- **`[\u00bf]` in List Literals** collapsed to `[]` on reparse, losing the fillable hole. Explicit `[?]` round-trips.\n- Stray trailing grouts in five hidden-test cells.\n\n## Tutorial-mode chrome\n\nAlso ports the styling/UX work from that branch:\n\n- a collapsible **Tasks** section, split from the prompt at its `Task` header (all 25 lessons now have one)\n- the hint as a keyed `<details>`, so its open state no longer leaks across slides\n- first/last slide nav gating \u2014 **required**, since `.hzt` `version` defaults to 1 and the old `version > 1` / `version < 10` gates would break\n- SAND background, focus-driven cell accent, `{{video:}}` and `{{no_editor}}` prompt markers\n- per-slide scroll memory, and driving the slide `<select>` from the model so it follows keyboard navigation\n- `Zipper.caret_to_start`, so `@code` loads with the caret at the start of the program\n\n`show_report` changes meaning under the new `show_task_ui` gate \u2014 it now marks a slide as a *task* (grading face + report icon) rather than \"start with the report panel expanded\" \u2014 so it is set on the six converted lessons that have real hidden tests. Only Probes, whose sole test is `test true end`, leaves it off.\n\nFour general CSS fixes come along: a broken pin-icon URL in `style.css` (which sits in `www/`, so `../img/` resolved outside it), the test sigil's `z-index` (it painted above projector overlays), `nowrap` on context-menu items, and overscroll containment so a nested horizontal scroll does not fire the browser back-gesture.\n\n## Deliberately left behind\n\n`TutorialProbeStrip` and `TutorialSlideInit` \u2014 both are exhaustive hardcoded tables over that branch's own slide ids and need `AutoProbe.t` plus new `ProbeProj.Settings` variants \u2014 and the probe/evaluator/Card rework they depend on.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `make dev` builds clean\n- [x] `make test-quick` \u2014 3465/3465\n- [x] `./hazel tutorial-verify` \u2014 25/25 slides round-trip cleanly\n- [x] All 25 lessons in the dropdown, in order, with their exact original titles\n- [x] Tables driven to 3/3 passing; Folding Lists to 3/3 (previously impossible)\n- [x] Tasks + Hint collapsibles, grading face and panel, prev/next gating, Task Reference sidebar\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
